#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:1
#: 2dd397f8d0ee4086b44d2fe7e865e4a3
msgid "Read the Mapflow processing results summary - feature counts, areas and lengths per layer, CSV export and questions to the Mapflow Agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:7
#: 64c8c5e2631a4108b48a79998857e91c
msgid "Results Summary (Statistics)"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:9
#: 3e1a70ab028a4c73accb53f7252e465c
msgid "Getting a vector layer is only part of the imagery analysis workflow. The next question is usually: *what did the model actually find?*"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:12
#: 1b495bad2d7043baade5d75d93ca971e
msgid "Every completed processing in Mapflow Web opens with an instant **summary** of its results – the number of detected features and their totals (area, length, counts) per output layer. The summary is calculated for the whole processing AOI, regardless of what is currently visible on the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:None
#: b05383cbf4fe437fb23a80b180b23945
msgid "Processing results with the summary panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:25
#: 2e8a3c4263c4403da5c8cdaea5782a2b
msgid "The service is powered by the **Statistics API** and is available for every default Mapflow model. Custom-model workflows include basic statistics, and their summaries can be customized as well (see :doc:`custom_pipelines`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:31
#: 7c5876ecfd694cbeb16e44be015490bb
msgid "The summary panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:33
#: 0c5f5514f3644666a509e983072487c5
msgid "When the processing is finished, the panel appears above the map with the total number of detected features, the list of the output layers and the processed area:"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:None
#: 2136415f274643519583f847729a08b4
msgid "Dataset ready - features detected"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:44
#: 53d006d4780b45a582a022ce077dfa5b
msgid "The panel contains:"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:46
#: db994f3760404056a4e76162691411e0
msgid "**Header** – the status of the dataset and the total number of detected features, e.g. *\"Dataset ready – 11,206 features detected\"*."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:48
#: da789eebd82b4ad99336f60484df4234
msgid "**Subtitle** – the output layers included in the processing and the size of the processed area, e.g. *\"crown · building · forest · roads · waterbodies over 1.00 km²\"*."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:50
#: b4ee0b5120244d11ad21deb0a767fdb9
msgid "**Per-layer statistics** – one entry per layer, colored as the layer on the map, with the feature count and the corresponding total (area or length)."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:52
#: 19d159e4a98b4e78b227b0a2dcaf9988
msgid "**Zoom hint** – tells you whether all the results are currently rendered on the map. At a low zoom level the map may display a part of the features, while the statistics are always counted for the whole result."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:55
#: 7a22e0c4ea4f4b97828eb3e67349f1b4
msgid "**Actions** – :ref:`Download CSV <statistics csv>` and :ref:`Ask about these results <statistics agent>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:57
#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:57
#: 9cc359b2cc7e4dc2887b6211f9fe45b3
#: d474f2758ad04b56983de56ad1647e7a
msgid "stats_button"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/results_summary.rst:61
#: dec8538c40814388a4ad59a16abf0057
msgid "If you closed the panel, or opened an earlier processing, you can bring the summary back with the **statistics** button |stats_button| in the toolbar under the map."
msgstr ""

